    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((-1) \\Diamond 6\\) using the operation \\(\\Diamond\\) defined by \\(a \\Diamond b = ab^2 - b + 1\\), we need to substitute \\(a = -1\\) and \\(b = 6\\) into the expression.\n\nFirst, let's substitute the values into the expression:\n\n\\[\n(-1) \\Diamond 6 = (-1) \\cdot 6^2 - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(6^2\\):\n\n\\[\n6^2 = 36\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\(36\\) back into the expression:\n\n\\[\n(-1) \\Diamond 6 = (-1) \\cdot 36 - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nPerform the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n(-1) \\cdot 36 = -36\n\\]\n\nSo the expression now is:\n\n\\[\n(-1) \\Diamond 6 = -36 - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nNext, perform the subtraction and addition from left to right:\n\n\\[\n-36 - 6 = -42\n\\]\n\nThen:\n\n\\[\n-42 + 1 = -41\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((-1) \\Diamond 6\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-41}\n\\]",
